    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37223" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέτι</span></b> , Prep. with gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέτι τοῦ ὅτε . .</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ever since</i> the time when .
			., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.106
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πατρῶν</span>
			<i>from</i> our fathers' time, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.245
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. νηπυτίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.791
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. κεῖθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					104
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. παίδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1549
				</span></i>
			: also in late Prose, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. νέου,
				ϝεαροῦ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				5.39
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. σπαργάνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.94
				</span></i>
			.</div>
